# Trivy ignore file — per-CVE exceptions with justifications
#
# This file documents individual CVE exceptions that cannot be addressed by
# version bumps or by the Rego policy (.trivy-ignore-policy.rego). Each entry
# MUST include a justification explaining why the CVE is accepted.
#
# Format: CVE-YYYY-NNNNN (one per line, # for comments)
# See: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#by-finding-ids
#
# Review cadence: Re-evaluate all entries quarterly or when the affected
# package is upgraded. Remove entries once the underlying package ships a fix.
#
# =============================================================================
#
# --- DeepVirFinder py3.6 sidecar (VEX: not-affected) -- reviewed 2026-08-19 ---
# This tool is not invoked by any HVP WDL task; the image exists only to keep
# DeepVirFinder available on demand. Its python=3.6 env (theano 1.0.3 + keras
# 2.2.4, per the upstream README) is EOL and cannot take patched keras/
# setuptools versions without abandoning the pinned, working tool. The keras
# deserialization CVEs require loading a malicious model; DeepVirFinder loads
# only its own bundled models and is fed nucleotide FASTA, never model files.
# Same exceptions the retired hvp-monolith already documented. exp forces
# quarterly re-review.
CVE-2024-3660 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2025-12060 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-11816 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-12481 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2024-6345 exp:2026-11-30
